    { "tool": "browser.open_url", "risk": "low", "domain": "windows", "params": ["platform", "external_account_id"],
      "verification": [],
      "_note": "v0.2 OAuth-assist: opens the enrolled device's default browser at a backend-constructed /oauth/:platform/connect link so a human sitting at THAT machine can complete platform consent using whatever session their own browser already has. tool-calls/service.ts overwrites/computes the `url` param server-side from platform+external_account_id before dispatch — a caller-supplied url is never trusted or forwarded. Deliberately does not automate the consent click itself (see docs/v0.2-marketing-ops-spec.md known gaps — that would violate Google/Meta OAuth app policy). No verification chain: whether the human actually clicks Allow is out of band, nothing server-side to re-check." },

    { "tool": "desktop.screenshot", "risk": "read", "domain": "windows_desktop", "params": [], "verification": [],
      "_note": "Computer-use addendum (docs/v0.1-computer-use-addendum.md). Auto-executes (read risk) — also used as the deterministic verification step for every write action below. Blocked entirely for tenants on ai_data_policy='no_screenshots' (policy-engine/index.ts), since there's no way to redact pixels the way text results are redacted." },
    { "tool": "desktop.move",       "risk": "read", "domain": "windows_desktop", "params": ["x", "y"], "verification": [],
      "_note": "Cursor move only, no state change — auto-executes like any other read tool. Not gated behind approval so the model can freely reposition without spamming a human for every glide." },
    { "tool": "desktop.wait",       "risk": "read", "domain": "windows_desktop", "params": ["ms"], "verification": [],
      "_note": "No-op delay the model can request between actions (e.g. waiting for a dialog to render). No device state effect." },
    { "tool": "desktop.click",        "risk": "high", "domain": "windows_desktop", "params": ["x", "y", "button"],
      "verification": ["desktop.screenshot"],
      "_note": "Computer-use addendum. risk:'high' means this NEVER auto-executes regardless of tenant autonomy opt-in (policy-engine/index.ts) — every click is held for human approval, by explicit user requirement, not inferred." },
    { "tool": "desktop.double_click", "risk": "high", "domain": "windows_desktop", "params": ["x", "y"],
      "verification": ["desktop.screenshot"] },
    { "tool": "desktop.drag",         "risk": "high", "domain": "windows_desktop", "params": ["path"],
      "verification": ["desktop.screenshot"] },
    { "tool": "desktop.keypress",     "risk": "high", "domain": "windows_desktop", "params": ["keys"],
      "verification": ["desktop.screenshot"],
      "_note": "agent/internal/tools/desktop_windows.go maps `keys` through an explicit virtual-key allowlist — an unrecognized key name fails closed, same principle as the tool-name allowlist itself." },
    { "tool": "desktop.type",         "risk": "high", "domain": "windows_desktop", "params": ["text"],
      "verification": ["desktop.screenshot"],
      "_note": "agent/internal/tools/desktop_windows.go hard-caps text length per call so one approved action has a bounded blast radius." },
    { "tool": "desktop.scroll",       "risk": "high", "domain": "windows_desktop", "params": ["x", "y", "scroll_x", "scroll_y"],
      "verification": ["desktop.screenshot"] },

    { "tool": "desktop.open_customer_view", "risk": "read", "domain": "windows_desktop", "params": [], "verification": [],
      "_note": "Not a computer-use action the AI decides to call — system-triggered once by computer-use/index.ts's startSession(), same as the initial desktop.screenshot. Opens the customer's own default browser to a read-only-plus-chat status page (frontend/src/app/tickets/:id/customer) so the person sitting at the machine can see what's happening and message the technician, without exposing approval controls. tool-calls/service.ts computes the url server-side from FRONTEND_URL + ticket id, same never-trust-the-caller pattern as browser.open_url." },

